WEBVTT

00:46.963 --> 00:48.381
Should I begin?

00:48.465 --> 00:49.424
MAY, 2011

00:49.507 --> 00:50.508
Well…

00:51.092 --> 00:52.761
Hello.

00:56.306 --> 00:58.308
My name is Choi Ung.

00:58.391 --> 00:59.893
CHOI UNG (19, MALE)

00:59.976 --> 01:01.352
Let's look at the first one.

01:01.436 --> 01:03.855
As limit x approaches one,

01:03.938 --> 01:06.566
you can find the limiting value.

01:06.649 --> 01:10.278
So we can think about
the case when it's smaller than one

01:10.361 --> 01:14.866
and when it's bigger than one. Understand?

01:14.949 --> 01:18.286
- Okay. When it's smaller than one…
- Don't look at the camera.

01:18.369 --> 01:21.539
- But it bothers me.
- Just act like it's not here.

01:21.623 --> 01:24.459
How can I? It's right in front of me.

01:24.542 --> 01:27.128
For this case, it goes down like this.

01:27.212 --> 01:29.506
- As you can see…
- So the answer is…

01:29.589 --> 01:31.132
I'm being filmed.

01:31.216 --> 01:32.801
You idiot. Look forward.

01:32.884 --> 01:34.886
Should we look at the next one?

01:34.969 --> 01:38.431
- The limiting value of this is one.
- But it's not just me.

01:38.515 --> 01:40.767
What are you looking at?
Look at the teacher.

01:40.850 --> 01:42.977
The limiting value of this is one as well.

01:43.061 --> 01:46.940
The limiting values of these are the same…

01:47.524 --> 01:49.150
This annoying brat as well.

01:49.234 --> 01:50.360
Let's end it here.

01:51.820 --> 01:53.613
Attention, bow.

01:54.197 --> 01:55.907
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

01:57.200 --> 01:58.660
Where are you going?

01:58.743 --> 02:01.454
It's none of your business.

02:06.459 --> 02:11.506
Sir, can we stop for a moment?
I can't keep working with that idiot.

02:12.632 --> 02:14.884
- "Idiot"?
- We've been filming for days.

02:14.968 --> 02:16.553
Why can't you sit still
when we're filming?

02:16.636 --> 02:19.180
I can't focus at all with you next to me.

02:19.264 --> 02:21.474
How can I
when there is a camera right next to me?

02:21.558 --> 02:24.269
Just focus on the class.
Can't you even do that?

02:24.352 --> 02:27.230
You can ignore me
and focus on class yourself.

02:27.313 --> 02:28.189
Can't you even do that?

02:28.273 --> 02:31.776
I guess you don't care because
your grades couldn't get any worse.

02:31.860 --> 02:34.445
But I won't let you bring down my grades.

02:37.031 --> 02:38.032
You heard her, right?

02:38.116 --> 02:41.494
Whatever. It's your social skills
that couldn't get any worse.

02:43.371 --> 02:44.747
Why did I agree to this?

02:44.831 --> 02:47.584
I know, right? Why did you agree to this?

02:50.170 --> 02:51.629
My name is Kook Yeon-su.

02:51.713 --> 02:52.547
KOOK YEON-SU (19, FEMALE)

02:53.172 --> 02:56.009
I think I first saw Choi Ung
in tenth grade.

02:58.177 --> 02:59.512
This much again?

02:59.596 --> 03:01.806
I'm reading less
because I have exams soon.

03:01.890 --> 03:05.018
You'll read all the books here
by the time you graduate.

03:05.101 --> 03:06.144
Kook Yeon-su…

03:07.562 --> 03:10.148
- Here. Enjoy.
- Thank you.

03:14.652 --> 03:16.487
APRIL'S TOP BOOKWORMS

03:16.571 --> 03:18.114
1ST: CHOI UNG
2ND: KOOK YEON-SU

03:20.450 --> 03:22.160
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

03:22.243 --> 03:23.703
Who is Choi Ung?

03:23.786 --> 03:25.455
He's in first place this month, too?

03:25.538 --> 03:27.248
Oh, Ung?

03:27.957 --> 03:29.626
I think he was over there.

03:33.880 --> 03:34.964
Hey.

03:36.591 --> 03:39.010
I met him somewhere that didn't suit him.

03:39.093 --> 03:40.470
I'm Kook Yeon-su from Class 5.

03:40.553 --> 03:42.263
What's your rank?

03:42.347 --> 03:44.057
- What rank?
- Your grades.

03:45.683 --> 03:46.851
I'm 267th.

03:48.436 --> 03:50.521
The total number of students here…

03:50.605 --> 03:52.607
There are 267 students.

03:53.942 --> 03:56.527
Back then, I just thought
that he was a strange kid.

04:01.407 --> 04:04.285
No, wait. That was the second time we met.

04:05.036 --> 04:07.121
The first time we met
was when we started high school.

04:07.205 --> 04:10.625
The student who entered with
the highest grades is Kook Yeon-su.

04:13.878 --> 04:15.338
Her name's Kook Yeon-su?

04:15.421 --> 04:17.090
What a funny name.

04:17.173 --> 04:21.177
I watched her because she walked
like she was entering a battlefield.

04:25.390 --> 04:27.767
HWIYEONG HIGH SCHOOL ENTRANCE CEREMONY

04:28.810 --> 04:30.645
Hey, look at her skirt.

04:30.728 --> 04:33.356
- She's obviously a teacher's pet.
- She's a stereotype.

04:33.439 --> 04:36.943
- They all have the same style.
- Hey, look at her shoes.

04:37.026 --> 04:38.987
Even my mom wouldn't wear that.

04:39.070 --> 04:41.948
- Spring is finally here.
- How tacky.

04:42.031 --> 04:44.492
The weather is still pretty cold.

04:44.575 --> 04:46.411
We met eyes for the first time,

04:46.494 --> 04:48.454
so I was trying to be nice by smiling.

04:48.538 --> 04:49.622
Hey.

04:49.706 --> 04:51.291
What are you looking at?

04:53.126 --> 04:56.129
But she seemed ill-tempered.

05:05.263 --> 05:09.267
Anyway, I thought I'd never
be involved with him again.

05:10.268 --> 05:11.561
You're here.

05:11.644 --> 05:13.396
Did you think about that offer?

05:13.479 --> 05:15.273
The producer's a friend of mine.

05:15.356 --> 05:16.774
He won't trouble you too much.

05:16.858 --> 05:19.068
You don't have to
if you think it will affect your grades.

05:19.736 --> 05:22.238
- Will it be just me?
- No, with one more student.

05:22.322 --> 05:26.284
It's a documentary where
they observe the best and worst students

05:26.367 --> 05:28.369
for a month as they spend time together.

05:29.370 --> 05:31.414
Anyway, just think about it.

05:36.711 --> 05:40.131
Will I be paid if I agree to do it?

05:40.214 --> 05:41.591
Of course.

05:47.346 --> 05:50.349
He was the exact opposite of me.

05:51.976 --> 05:54.771
Oh, you're here already.

05:54.854 --> 05:56.022
- Hang on.
- All right.

05:56.105 --> 05:58.900
Just a moment.

05:58.983 --> 06:02.028
The ingredients must be here.
Check them thoroughly.

06:02.111 --> 06:04.280
They were in a bad condition last time.

06:04.363 --> 06:06.240
- Check them properly.
- All right.

06:06.324 --> 06:10.787
SEAFOOD SOUP WITH UNG
POTATO SOUP WITH UNG

06:10.870 --> 06:12.413
CHICKEN FEET WITH UNG

06:12.497 --> 06:14.874
- Hello.
- Hello.

06:14.957 --> 06:17.668
He's Ung's father.

06:17.752 --> 06:19.670
- Hello.
- Hello.

06:20.254 --> 06:21.380
Ung!

06:21.464 --> 06:23.382
- Hey. Come over here.
- But things happened

06:23.466 --> 06:25.927
regardless of my intentions.

06:26.010 --> 06:28.012
Why didn't you tell us
about the documentary?

06:28.096 --> 06:30.056
I said I wouldn't do it.

06:30.139 --> 06:33.726
The producer came all the way here.
Why did you say no?

06:33.810 --> 06:36.437
And it's with
the top student in your year.

06:36.521 --> 06:37.772
Of course you should do it!

06:37.855 --> 06:41.943
Of course! We don't know
what he's doing at school.

06:42.026 --> 06:44.487
If you film that,
we'll be able to see what he does.

06:44.570 --> 06:46.656
- That's right.
- Thank you.

06:46.739 --> 06:48.616
- Thank you.
- I said I'm not doing it!

06:48.699 --> 06:50.159
Why would you refuse?

06:50.243 --> 06:53.162
Why would I do that?
I don't want everyone to know my face.

06:53.246 --> 06:55.706
You'll be able
to build a great memory with this.

06:55.790 --> 06:57.625
- Right.
- I'm a senior now, you know.

06:57.708 --> 07:00.002
Don't you think it will affect my grades?

07:01.838 --> 07:03.089
What's he on about?

07:03.172 --> 07:05.967
They are letting you study
with the top student in your grade.

07:06.050 --> 07:07.718
You should be grateful!

07:07.802 --> 07:08.719
I mean…

07:08.803 --> 07:11.597
It was as if it had to happen.

07:11.681 --> 07:13.724
She's kind of weird!

07:14.350 --> 07:17.478
Anyway, that's how it all started.

07:22.358 --> 07:26.195
Choi Ung from Class 1
will be joining us for a month.

07:26.279 --> 07:27.113
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

07:27.196 --> 07:28.489
Be nice to him.

07:28.573 --> 07:32.243
It may be distracting for you
since they'll be filming,

07:32.326 --> 07:34.287
but it will be a fun experience.

07:34.370 --> 07:38.958
And with that,
I hope you all have a great day.

07:39.041 --> 07:40.001
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

08:04.108 --> 08:06.402
It was more bothersome than I thought.

08:18.414 --> 08:20.541
The worst students make the most fuss.

08:22.251 --> 08:24.837
- Are you talking to me?
- Keep your stuff off my desk.

08:35.431 --> 08:39.101
She was way more annoying than I thought.

08:46.275 --> 08:49.153
At first, I tried
to become friends with her.

08:49.237 --> 08:50.363
Hey…

09:19.308 --> 09:21.018
Can we…

09:28.818 --> 09:30.236
I said I was sorry.

09:31.862 --> 09:33.531
I'm not sorry.

09:35.575 --> 09:36.742
But what can I do?

09:37.493 --> 09:38.786
We're just so different.

09:40.621 --> 09:41.706
No! Not here!

09:43.416 --> 09:44.584
Darn it.

09:45.334 --> 09:46.419
Go!

09:48.129 --> 09:49.255
Here.

09:53.301 --> 09:54.969
- Hey.
- Over here!

09:57.722 --> 09:58.848
Oh, my.

09:59.599 --> 10:01.225
Darn it. Hey!

10:01.934 --> 10:02.852
Oh, gosh!

10:11.319 --> 10:12.862
Are you okay?

10:18.826 --> 10:20.786
He's so childish.

10:21.621 --> 10:22.622
Ma'am.

10:23.706 --> 10:27.084
How can I solve that
with the L'Hôpital's rule?

10:28.711 --> 10:29.837
Ma'am.

10:30.379 --> 10:34.091
Can we solve this
by using the derived function?

10:34.175 --> 10:35.217
- Ma'am.
- Yes?

10:35.301 --> 10:37.762
- Ma'am.
- All right, kids. Enjoy your lunch.

10:37.845 --> 10:39.096
Ma'am.

10:40.222 --> 10:42.600
She's so selfish.

10:42.683 --> 10:43.684
Ma'am.

10:44.268 --> 10:45.770
THE UNBEARABLE LIGHTNESS OF BEING

10:47.480 --> 10:49.523
I love lying in the shade.

10:50.900 --> 10:52.443
The gentle breeze,

10:53.903 --> 10:55.738
the sunlight shining through the trees…

10:59.325 --> 11:01.160
You're so ridiculous.

11:03.287 --> 11:04.205
Can you move?

11:04.288 --> 11:07.416
Finish reading that
and return it to the library.

11:15.508 --> 11:16.801
This is so nice.

11:18.052 --> 11:20.137
He's so lazy.

11:40.241 --> 11:41.117
Who was that?

11:42.743 --> 11:44.703
Choi Ung! You again?

11:45.371 --> 11:46.747
I told you to be quiet!

11:48.457 --> 11:50.084
Things are already exhausting,

11:50.167 --> 11:52.545
but she just makes it worse.

11:52.628 --> 11:55.673
He's just so pathetic.

11:59.802 --> 12:01.470
Sorry. What was the question?

12:01.554 --> 12:03.514
Pay attention.

12:05.349 --> 12:07.143
Oh, things I hate?

12:07.226 --> 12:08.394
Kook Yeon-su.

12:12.148 --> 12:14.692
I mean, I hate Kook Yeong-su.
She's some girl I know.

12:14.775 --> 12:19.321
I hate pathetic beings.
I hate everyone who's pathetic.

12:19.405 --> 12:21.365
Being selfish. I hate selfish people who--

12:21.449 --> 12:23.200
People who cause trouble for others.

12:23.284 --> 12:26.871
Why can't they just keep to themselves
and not drag others down with them?

12:26.954 --> 12:28.164
Being harsh.

12:28.247 --> 12:29.832
Some people talk without thinking.

12:29.915 --> 12:31.500
They don't think at all.

12:31.584 --> 12:33.127
Look who's talking.

12:33.210 --> 12:36.505
He just doesn't think at all.

12:36.589 --> 12:39.425
Wait. Are you talking about me?

12:39.508 --> 12:41.760
You seemed to be talking about me too.

12:41.844 --> 12:44.013
What? Are you kidding me?

12:44.096 --> 12:45.431
No, I'm totally serious.

12:46.640 --> 12:49.101
Why are you filming this again?

12:49.185 --> 12:52.229
It's a show where the top student helps
the student at the bottom of the class.

12:52.313 --> 12:54.106
- Right?
- I see.

12:54.190 --> 12:55.191
Is this some kind of a test

12:55.274 --> 12:57.526
to see how long you can withstand
someone who has no social skills?

12:57.610 --> 13:00.905
Doing experiments like that
is pretty unethical.

13:00.988 --> 13:04.992
The best student and the worst student.
Which is more anti-social?

13:05.075 --> 13:06.994
When people like her enter society,

13:07.077 --> 13:09.747
they will only tire out
the people around them.

13:09.830 --> 13:12.958
Well, you wouldn't even
be able to participate in society.

13:13.042 --> 13:14.752
How would you know?

13:17.588 --> 13:21.759
What do you think
you'll be like in ten years?

13:25.638 --> 13:28.057
In ten years, I'll be 29.

13:29.308 --> 13:32.561
I'm sure I'd be good at
whatever I'm doing.

13:33.562 --> 13:36.690
I want to live a peaceful life
without doing anything.

13:36.774 --> 13:40.736
I'll be leading people around me,
living an active life.

13:40.819 --> 13:41.779
A successful life.

13:41.862 --> 13:44.740
I hope I'll live a quiet life.

13:44.823 --> 13:47.034
- Anyway…
- One thing I know for sure is that--

13:47.117 --> 13:49.578
…I won't have to see
this annoying face again.

13:50.538 --> 13:52.248
That's what I wanted to say.

13:56.210 --> 13:57.711
THE BEST AND WORST STUDENTS
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

13:57.795 --> 13:59.255
VIEWS

13:59.338 --> 14:00.339
DOCUMENTARIES

14:04.301 --> 14:05.261
LEAVING A REPLY BECAUSE NO ONE WOULD

14:06.512 --> 14:07.596
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

14:12.893 --> 14:14.645
TRENDING VIDEO
SO FUNNY

14:22.486 --> 14:23.946
AMAZING CHEMISTRY
HILARIOUS

14:25.447 --> 14:27.992
THIS IS A MUST WATCH
PLEASE LET THERE BE A SECOND SEASON

14:36.125 --> 14:38.294
EPISODE 1
I KNOW WHAT YOU DID LAST SUMMER

14:41.088 --> 14:42.172
This isn't it.

14:42.256 --> 14:43.090
THE PRESENT

14:43.173 --> 14:44.508
Ms. Kook Yeon-su?

14:46.051 --> 14:46.886
Yes.

14:46.969 --> 14:50.598
I don't think you have
anything more to add. Will you continue?

14:50.681 --> 14:53.767
This isn't the life I thought I'd live.

14:55.561 --> 14:59.440
But still, please listen
until the end and give me your opinion.

15:00.024 --> 15:02.026
All right, then. Continue.

15:02.109 --> 15:04.486
I will explain
the online promotion methods.

15:04.570 --> 15:08.032
We're planning on gaining
people's interest before the opening

15:08.115 --> 15:11.535
through online campaigns
and participation events.

15:11.619 --> 15:13.954
And through hashtag events--

15:14.038 --> 15:15.080
Ms. Kook.

15:15.164 --> 15:17.166
This is pretty disappointing.

15:17.249 --> 15:19.209
This isn't what we asked for.

15:19.293 --> 15:21.086
You should have
checked with us in advance.

15:21.170 --> 15:24.214
Your ideas are too mediocre.

15:24.298 --> 15:27.551
To attract people's interests
before the store opens,

15:27.635 --> 15:30.596
- we should do online--
- Don't you think I know that?

15:30.679 --> 15:33.223
- But we--
- Your company's name is Run, right?

15:33.307 --> 15:34.433
You're a small company,

15:34.516 --> 15:37.019
but you won quite a lot of awards,

15:37.102 --> 15:39.396
and I heard you're
quite famous in the industry.

15:40.147 --> 15:42.066
But your work is pathetic.

15:42.149 --> 15:45.152
You've built up a great image
for your company, I'll give you that.

15:45.986 --> 15:48.781
Ji-hyeon. The presentation this afternoon…

15:48.864 --> 15:50.908
Can we reschedule it to 10 a.m.?

15:50.991 --> 15:53.327
- Mr. Jang.
- Yes? You're done, right?

15:53.410 --> 15:54.411
Is there anything else?

15:54.495 --> 15:59.375
Getting looked down on like this
was never part of my plan.

15:59.458 --> 16:02.503
- Yes. I'm not done yet.
- Hurry up, then.

16:11.053 --> 16:13.931
Offline,
we'll be collaborating with an artist

16:14.014 --> 16:15.891
for the opening of Soen Shop.

16:15.975 --> 16:18.477
Isn't it cliché to use merch
to attract customers?

16:18.560 --> 16:21.730
It isn't very effective
and is a waste of resources.

16:21.814 --> 16:23.023
Consumers won't fall for--

16:24.274 --> 16:27.611
Didn't you say you'd listen
until the end, Mr. Jang?

16:30.030 --> 16:31.031
Go on.

16:31.824 --> 16:35.077
This isn't just so that we could
lure in customers with the merchandise.

16:35.160 --> 16:39.540
We'll be merchandising the shop itself
to promote the company.

16:41.750 --> 16:45.462
These are the works of Go-oh,
the most popular illustrator these days.

16:45.546 --> 16:49.800
Go-oh is known for drawing detailed
and trendy pieces based on buildings.

16:49.883 --> 16:54.346
And recently, Go-oh received attention
as the idol singer NJ bought one of them.

16:55.139 --> 16:56.849
Through this collaboration,

16:56.932 --> 16:59.935
we'll host a live drawing show
for the opening ceremony.

17:01.603 --> 17:02.980
Go on.

17:03.063 --> 17:06.942
The artist's image matches
the unique and innovative goods

17:07.026 --> 17:10.112
that Soen Shop aims
to provide its customers.

17:10.195 --> 17:13.574
Go-oh already has a large fanbase
because of his unique drawings

17:13.657 --> 17:16.035
and his sincere attitude toward art.

17:16.118 --> 17:18.871
If we promote the shop
with his drawing on the exterior wall,

17:18.954 --> 17:23.500
I'm sure it will make Soen Shop
the hottest place to visit.

17:31.133 --> 17:32.801
Can you get the artist on board?

17:33.552 --> 17:35.137
Of course. It won't be a problem.

17:35.220 --> 17:36.972
You'd better be right.

17:38.640 --> 17:40.017
ARTIST GO-OH

17:40.100 --> 17:41.310
Not bad.

17:42.144 --> 17:45.355
I don't know why you waited
until the last minute to show us that.

17:45.439 --> 17:46.982
- The order--
- You can proceed.

18:02.623 --> 18:06.085
Ms. Kook. That was great.
You were so cool today.

18:06.168 --> 18:10.422
I heard Mr. Jang is very aggressive.
He sure was scary.

18:10.506 --> 18:12.299
He's doing that on purpose.

18:12.382 --> 18:15.344
He called us over this early
so he could have the upper hand.

18:15.427 --> 18:17.096
He even kept cutting her off.

18:17.179 --> 18:19.431
But still,
we have this project in the bag now.

18:19.515 --> 18:23.393
But Ms. Kook. Can we really
get the artist to work with us?

18:23.477 --> 18:26.772
I thought that wasn't confirmed yet.

18:27.856 --> 18:29.608
That jerk…

18:36.115 --> 18:39.618
When we get back to the office,
get me all the data on the artist.

18:39.701 --> 18:42.079
Everything from his social media
to his interviews.

18:42.162 --> 18:44.748
We have to do this project no matter what.

18:45.415 --> 18:48.544
But the artist is known
for being a recluse.

18:48.627 --> 18:51.672
Nobody's seen his face,
even at exhibitions.

18:52.172 --> 18:55.217
I'm going to find him, no matter what.

18:58.512 --> 19:01.098
How could he cut me off like that?

19:01.181 --> 19:03.142
Did he never learn any manners?

19:03.809 --> 19:05.561
Jeez, where is my car?

19:24.037 --> 19:25.330
Mr. Jang.

19:26.248 --> 19:28.333
Did you have something to say to me?

19:30.836 --> 19:33.005
Are you opening my car door for me?

19:33.088 --> 19:34.047
What?

19:41.597 --> 19:44.975
I'm sorry. I haven't gotten used
to the company car yet.

19:45.058 --> 19:46.101
I was mistaken.

19:47.978 --> 19:50.564
- Ms. Kook.
- Yes?

19:50.647 --> 19:52.274
I hate baseless courage.

19:53.025 --> 19:55.861
I think irresponsible people
are the most pathetic.

19:56.653 --> 19:59.031
- Right.
- I hope you weren't bluffing

19:59.114 --> 20:01.366
when you said you could
get the artist on board.

20:01.450 --> 20:03.619
You're not that pathetic, are you?

20:18.884 --> 20:20.802
Ten years ago…

20:20.886 --> 20:22.137
That jerk…

20:22.221 --> 20:25.599
…I would have never imagined

20:25.682 --> 20:27.559
that I'd be treated this way.

20:36.193 --> 20:38.362
I had always known

20:39.571 --> 20:41.740
that my life would be peaceful.

20:45.661 --> 20:47.788
I've always dreamed of this.

20:48.664 --> 20:52.292
We started a restaurant
for drivers passing by.

20:52.376 --> 20:53.877
- Hang on.
- Why?

20:53.961 --> 20:55.963
Wait. What's he doing?

20:56.046 --> 20:58.548
Stop acting so weird back there.

20:58.632 --> 21:00.926
I have to film Dad,
but you're being distracting.

21:01.009 --> 21:03.720
You ruined the shot. It's your fault.

21:03.804 --> 21:06.306
Stop bothering us and go inside.

21:06.390 --> 21:08.225
But I was here first.

21:08.308 --> 21:10.978
I thought I'd be fine talking
in front of the camera,

21:11.061 --> 21:12.562
but it's quite nerve-racking.

21:12.646 --> 21:16.149
- I want a little more peace though.
- Our franchise began

21:16.233 --> 21:20.946
as a diner for drivers 25 years ago.

21:21.029 --> 21:25.325
We specialized in
steamed fish and chicken feet.

21:25.409 --> 21:27.953
- Then word got around--
- Stop it already!

21:28.036 --> 21:29.246
You ruined the shot!

21:29.329 --> 21:31.415
He's a busy man, you know.

21:31.498 --> 21:33.417
Ung, you should go.
Aren't you late for work?

21:33.500 --> 21:34.626
It's fine. I have time.

21:34.710 --> 21:36.336
Then eat something before you go.

21:37.629 --> 21:38.839
Don't you dare!

21:38.922 --> 21:40.132
You little brat.

21:40.215 --> 21:42.134
Stop loafing around and work on this.

21:42.217 --> 21:45.095
Don't you think I'm busy too?

21:45.178 --> 21:46.263
- Nonsense.
- Ridiculous.

21:46.847 --> 21:49.266
You? Busy? You're not even working.

21:49.349 --> 21:50.809
- Hey, put that away.
- Come on.

21:50.892 --> 21:53.312
He's spending
his precious time helping us.

21:53.395 --> 21:54.855
You should be thanking him.

21:54.938 --> 21:56.356
You little brat.

21:56.440 --> 21:58.692
Finish up and watch the counter.

21:58.775 --> 21:59.735
And don't run away.

21:59.818 --> 22:01.737
- Honey, help me with something.
- Wait, I…

22:01.820 --> 22:02.988
I can't do it by myself.

22:03.071 --> 22:05.449
Jeez. I'd better go.

22:06.950 --> 22:08.910
I told you to stop filming.

22:08.994 --> 22:12.247
You'd better stop if you don't
want to lose your fingers or the camera.

22:12.831 --> 22:14.624
What happened to your face?

22:15.625 --> 22:19.129
- Even pork is marinated for eight hours.
- What do you mean?

22:19.212 --> 22:21.298
I only slept
two and a half hours last night.

22:21.381 --> 22:23.091
I got less rest than pork.

22:23.175 --> 22:27.012
That's too bad. You sleep and poop
as much as a pig though.

22:27.095 --> 22:28.805
Shut up. And stop filming!

22:29.514 --> 22:32.517
But I was told to film you too
for the promotional video.

22:32.601 --> 22:34.186
No way. Don't you dare.

22:34.269 --> 22:35.604
Ung!

22:35.687 --> 22:36.605
- Yes?
- Yes?

22:36.688 --> 22:37.814
Ung.

22:38.774 --> 22:40.150
Over here. Look at the camera.

22:42.194 --> 22:43.236
That's right.

22:44.321 --> 22:45.280
How cute.

22:50.535 --> 22:52.245
- Look over here.
- Ung! Look at Mommy.

22:52.329 --> 22:53.371
- Ung! Over here.
- That's right.

22:53.455 --> 22:55.332
- Look at your teacher.
- How cute!

22:55.415 --> 22:56.458
Hang on.

22:56.541 --> 22:58.251
Look at your teacher. Yes, good.

22:58.335 --> 23:00.045
- Look over there.
- He grew a lot.

23:00.128 --> 23:02.089
- It must be because your husband is tall.
- Look at your teacher.

23:02.172 --> 23:03.882
Is he listening to his teacher?

23:03.965 --> 23:05.383
I bought this for today.

23:05.467 --> 23:07.260
"Choi Ung"?

23:07.344 --> 23:10.305
Yes. I'm Choi Ung. What's your name?

23:10.388 --> 23:11.848
I'm not going to tell you.

23:15.310 --> 23:16.228
KIM JI-UNG

23:16.311 --> 23:17.521
Not you. Ji-ung.

23:17.604 --> 23:18.772
Do you want some stew?

23:18.855 --> 23:20.941
- Yes, I'd love that.
- What about me?

23:21.024 --> 23:22.359
You can have some too.

23:23.777 --> 23:26.488
Hey, I've been thinking…

23:26.571 --> 23:28.865
I'll practice my lines properly,

23:28.949 --> 23:32.202
so would it be okay
to do this again when you have time?

23:32.285 --> 23:35.664
Anytime is fine with me.
So call me when you want to do it.

23:36.665 --> 23:40.836
Thank you so much.
It's so nice having a producer help out.

23:40.919 --> 23:42.796
When else would I be able to try this?

23:44.798 --> 23:47.008
Dad. Don't look at me like that.

23:47.092 --> 23:49.010
The cabbages are arriving later, okay?

23:49.094 --> 23:52.055
Don't you dare think about running away
and move them inside.

23:52.764 --> 23:55.600
I hope you're not forgetting
that I'm your son!

23:56.852 --> 23:59.062
- Have two bowls, alright?
- Okay.

23:59.604 --> 24:03.733
It seems like you'll be the one
inheriting the restaurant later.

24:03.817 --> 24:06.403
My parents are acting
like you're their son these days.

24:07.279 --> 24:09.239
But think about it.

24:09.322 --> 24:11.491
I act more like their son than you.

24:11.575 --> 24:12.617
Jeez.

24:12.701 --> 24:14.077
Aren't you working these days?

24:14.161 --> 24:17.080
Why do you keep lurking around here
and threatening my status?

24:17.164 --> 24:19.916
I finally got a short vacation
after finishing a program.

24:20.000 --> 24:23.128
I'll be busy again
when I start my next project.

24:23.211 --> 24:25.630
I should have fun here before that.

24:25.714 --> 24:28.592
Hey! What do you think you're doing?

24:28.675 --> 24:30.969
- I'm having fun.
- You jerk!

24:31.052 --> 24:33.972
Wait! Father, look at Ung
holding the bean sprouts like that!

24:34.055 --> 24:35.807
- I wasn't--
- Put that down!

24:35.891 --> 24:37.184
Put it down.

24:37.267 --> 24:38.685
- Put it down!
- Don't play around with that!

24:38.768 --> 24:39.978
You're dead, you jerk!

24:40.061 --> 24:42.689
- How can you be so childish?
- My goodness.

24:42.772 --> 24:44.191
You're a grown-up, you know!

24:44.274 --> 24:48.695
I thought I'd have matured
a bit more than this though.

24:50.322 --> 24:53.533
Ms. Kook and Mr. Jang
were clashing since they're so similar.

24:53.617 --> 24:56.578
It's so fun watching them argue.

24:56.661 --> 24:59.581
You saw how Ms. Kook reacted
when Mr. Jang cut her off

24:59.664 --> 25:01.666
during her presentation, right?

25:02.375 --> 25:05.754
"Didn't you say you'd listen
until the end, Mr. Jang?" Unbelievable.

25:05.837 --> 25:08.465
But still, Ms. Kook was so cool.
Don't you think so?

25:08.548 --> 25:09.925
She's cool.

25:10.008 --> 25:13.011
It wasn't something a small company
like us can easily get.

25:13.094 --> 25:15.138
But she's getting that opportunity for us.

25:15.222 --> 25:17.682
She's almost like
the breadwinner of this family.

25:17.766 --> 25:19.643
Our CEO's good luck charm.

25:19.726 --> 25:22.270
But imagine if we get on her bad side.

25:22.354 --> 25:25.857
She's so dependable
when she's fighting our clients,

25:25.941 --> 25:27.734
but if she ever gets angry at us…

25:27.817 --> 25:29.861
Polar bears tear people apart
with their paws,

25:29.945 --> 25:32.906
but Ms. Kook tears people with her words…
How did it go, Ms. Kook?

25:33.490 --> 25:36.284
The data I asked for on Go-oh.

25:36.368 --> 25:37.994
Have them ready by 3 p.m.

25:38.078 --> 25:39.329
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay.

25:43.291 --> 25:46.294
What's going on here? What is it?

25:46.378 --> 25:48.296
Why are you guys so good?

25:48.380 --> 25:50.423
I heard you were given the green light.

25:50.507 --> 25:52.342
I was so shocked.

25:52.926 --> 25:53.969
Good work.

25:54.052 --> 25:58.265
And I can't believe Ms. Kook
succeeded again.

25:58.348 --> 26:00.141
Today's a day to celebrate.

26:00.225 --> 26:01.768
- We should--
- No gatherings.

26:01.851 --> 26:03.395
I'm not suggesting a team dinner.

26:03.478 --> 26:05.272
Why would we do such a thing?

26:05.355 --> 26:08.441
We shouldn't be having
a company gathering at a time like this.

26:08.525 --> 26:09.651
We all hate it.

26:10.568 --> 26:11.820
Then how about

26:11.903 --> 26:13.738
- dinner--
- How about lunch instead?

26:13.822 --> 26:16.616
You don't want to waste
your dinnertime with me?

26:16.700 --> 26:18.994
That's not what I mean.
It's going to be hard

26:19.077 --> 26:20.870
to get off work on time.

26:20.954 --> 26:22.747
Then should we go have lunch now?

26:23.623 --> 26:25.292
We already had lunch, sir.

26:28.044 --> 26:29.462
What do you mean?

26:29.546 --> 26:30.630
I just remembered

26:30.714 --> 26:34.050
that we all had lunch together
on the way back.

26:36.303 --> 26:39.681
What about me? Why didn't you invite me?

26:39.764 --> 26:44.019
You didn't attend the presentation
because you had a stomachache.

26:44.102 --> 26:46.688
So we thought you'd skip lunch.

26:47.689 --> 26:49.524
Right. That was smart thinking.

26:50.191 --> 26:52.986
Then you don't want dinner,
and you already ate lunch.

26:53.069 --> 26:54.237
What should I do, then?

26:54.321 --> 26:56.948
Then how about some coffee?

26:57.032 --> 26:58.450
- Yes.
- Coffee sounds great.

26:58.533 --> 27:00.577
- You all have coffee.
- We have coffee.

27:01.202 --> 27:02.454
You already have coffee.

27:03.121 --> 27:04.414
You all have some.

27:04.497 --> 27:05.999
- Yes.
- Fine.

27:06.082 --> 27:08.710
- Why don't I get you some porridge, then?
- Don't worry.

27:10.920 --> 27:12.005
I hate porridge.

27:13.506 --> 27:14.674
He seems upset.

27:27.437 --> 27:29.272
SOL-I

27:35.487 --> 27:42.494
SEOUL HARDWARE STORE

30:11.392 --> 30:12.519
What is it?

30:12.602 --> 30:14.729
You wench! Why weren't you picking up?

30:17.982 --> 30:20.193
Why weren't you picking up?

30:20.276 --> 30:22.862
Jeez. Don't you see that I'm working?

30:22.946 --> 30:25.114
But still, you should answer your phone.

30:25.198 --> 30:26.950
Darn it…

30:27.033 --> 30:28.117
What?

30:28.618 --> 30:30.912
What are you doing? Hey!

30:30.995 --> 30:32.205
Get up. Exercise time.

30:32.288 --> 30:34.290
Hey! What do you think you're doing?

30:34.374 --> 30:36.835
Get up. You said you're not sleeping well.

30:36.918 --> 30:38.711
Stop it! Let go of me!

30:40.088 --> 30:43.925
It's the manager's job
to take care of the artist's health too.

30:46.386 --> 30:49.013
I'm already exhausted,
and he makes it worse.

30:49.556 --> 30:51.683
Aren't I a great manager? I'm so kind.

30:51.766 --> 30:52.934
You're fired.

30:53.017 --> 30:54.602
That counts as wrongful dismissal.

30:54.686 --> 30:57.063
We'll stop when we
make it over there. You can do it.

30:57.146 --> 30:58.314
I can't.

30:58.398 --> 30:59.858
You have to go. Come on.

30:59.941 --> 31:01.317
- Jeez.
- One, two, three, four.

31:01.401 --> 31:02.694
Two, two, three, four.

31:02.777 --> 31:04.946
All right! We're here!

31:05.029 --> 31:06.447
Over here. Hurry up.

31:06.531 --> 31:07.949
Hey! What's that?

31:08.032 --> 31:09.450
The flag. Make the goal.

31:09.951 --> 31:13.204
- There you go.
- Yes, goal!

31:15.915 --> 31:18.167
You guys are doing all kinds
of stupid things.

31:18.251 --> 31:20.587
I heard you only slept
two and a half hours.

31:20.670 --> 31:23.631
- You have such a big mouth.
- Me? Take this.

31:23.715 --> 31:24.924
Gosh.

31:25.008 --> 31:27.302
Aren't you supposed to be busy?
Did you get fired?

31:27.385 --> 31:29.929
Hey, if you're skilled,
you can slack off all you want.

31:31.472 --> 31:35.476
Right. Did you still not
tell your parents what you do?

31:35.560 --> 31:37.437
They just know I'm drawing.

31:37.520 --> 31:40.857
They called me a while ago
and asked if you make enough money

31:40.940 --> 31:43.443
since they couldn't find anything
when they searched your name.

31:43.526 --> 31:44.944
Didn't you tell them anything?

31:45.028 --> 31:47.572
How much do you earn? Tell me.

31:47.655 --> 31:49.741
You're not even telling your family?

31:49.824 --> 31:51.826
You're being overly secretive.

31:51.910 --> 31:54.245
- Darn it.
- Jeez!

31:54.329 --> 31:57.540
- You shook it, didn't you?
- No. So how much does he earn?

31:57.624 --> 31:59.918
Each drawing sells for…

32:01.169 --> 32:02.837
- What? For real?
- Yes.

32:03.546 --> 32:04.380
Son of a bitch.

32:05.590 --> 32:08.843
Hey. You just
wanted to swear at me, right?

32:08.927 --> 32:09.886
Of course not.

32:09.969 --> 32:12.180
Son of a bitch. What?

32:13.181 --> 32:16.434
Oh, right. I told Father
that you didn't move the cabbages.

32:16.517 --> 32:18.061
He said he'll kill you tomorrow.

32:18.144 --> 32:20.605
- Oh, my. What are you going to do?
- Darn it.

32:27.153 --> 32:29.113
Why is the weather so nice today?

32:38.206 --> 32:39.832
- Jeez!
- Jeez!

32:39.916 --> 32:41.793
You idiots.

32:41.876 --> 32:44.963
- You shook these, didn't you?
- Didn't you see what happened to mine?

32:45.672 --> 32:48.007
Did I shake them? Did you?

32:48.091 --> 32:49.050
No way.

32:50.885 --> 32:53.179
You're ignoring me again, aren't you?

32:56.265 --> 32:57.392
You asshole.

32:58.893 --> 33:02.355
You really have no customers.
You might go out of business soon.

33:02.438 --> 33:04.524
- Hey!
- Gosh, you startled me.

33:04.607 --> 33:06.943
I can hear you
even if you whisper, you know.

33:07.026 --> 33:10.488
Do you know how many times
you've stood that guy up?

33:12.031 --> 33:13.700
- Three times?
- It's four.

33:13.783 --> 33:16.285
Do you have
some kind of grudge against him?

33:16.369 --> 33:18.579
How could I?
I've never even seen him before.

33:18.663 --> 33:22.166
But you bailed on him when he said
he'd come to your office building?

33:22.250 --> 33:26.546
He even went there during lunchtime
because you said you were so busy.

33:26.629 --> 33:28.006
I totally forgot.

33:28.756 --> 33:30.258
You're such a scumbag.

33:30.925 --> 33:32.885
How can you be so arrogant?

33:32.969 --> 33:35.680
How can you function as a member
of society like that?

33:36.389 --> 33:38.933
People worse than me
are living normal lives in society.

33:39.517 --> 33:42.353
Shut up. That guy you bailed on four times

33:42.437 --> 33:44.188
must be totally smitten with you.

33:44.272 --> 33:46.524
He says he really wants to meet you.

33:46.607 --> 33:47.942
I pity him so much.

33:48.568 --> 33:51.154
- Is that so?
- "Is that so?"

33:51.237 --> 33:52.572
You have to see him this time.

33:52.655 --> 33:55.950
If you bail on him again,
I'm going to cut ties with you.

33:56.034 --> 33:57.535
All right. I'll go see him.

33:59.120 --> 34:00.621
I'm sick of this.

34:00.705 --> 34:02.165
I'm not telling you to date him.

34:02.248 --> 34:05.376
Just meet some guys.
At least give it a go.

34:05.460 --> 34:07.754
Office, home, and here.
You don't go anywhere else.

34:07.837 --> 34:10.465
Your eyes look soulless and empty.

34:10.548 --> 34:12.258
There's probably nothing under your skin.

34:13.342 --> 34:14.427
Skin!

34:15.094 --> 34:16.512
I want some pork skin. Cook me some.

34:16.596 --> 34:18.598
My gosh. It's like talking to a wall.

34:19.474 --> 34:21.684
Let's live soulful lives.

34:21.768 --> 34:24.228
Is meeting guys
your idea of a soulful life?

34:24.312 --> 34:25.897
Forget it. I'm just going to work.

34:25.980 --> 34:28.608
- Meet someone at work then.
- That's horrible.

34:28.691 --> 34:30.443
You're making me lose my appetite.

34:30.526 --> 34:31.444
Then…

34:32.862 --> 34:34.864
Could it be that
you still haven't got over--

34:34.947 --> 34:37.492
Gosh. So this is how you
drive away your customers.

34:37.575 --> 34:39.619
- I'm leaving.
- All right, I'll stop. I'm sorry.

34:39.702 --> 34:42.163
Please sit down, ma'am. I'm sorry.

34:43.706 --> 34:45.541
You have such a bad temper.

34:49.170 --> 34:50.254
My gosh.

34:53.966 --> 34:56.302
Let me take a break. Jeez.

34:56.385 --> 34:57.970
Why are you so bad?

34:58.054 --> 34:59.806
You try it then.

34:59.889 --> 35:00.932
Goodness.

35:03.476 --> 35:05.478
Ung. That live drawing show--

35:05.561 --> 35:06.687
I'm not doing it.

35:06.771 --> 35:07.855
Darn it.

35:07.939 --> 35:10.942
Why are you so obsessed
with keeping your identity hidden?

35:11.025 --> 35:14.320
You're living in the past.
It's all about communication these days.

35:14.403 --> 35:17.573
He's not suited for that.
He can't even talk properly.

35:17.657 --> 35:19.158
I really don't get it.

35:19.242 --> 35:21.202
Five years ago, all you did was draw,

35:21.285 --> 35:23.121
saying that you were going to succeed.

35:23.204 --> 35:26.124
But now you're rejecting opportunities.
What are you thinking?

35:26.207 --> 35:29.460
He's changed now that he's successful.
He's full of himself.

35:29.544 --> 35:31.546
- Hey.
- You shouldn't be so arrogant.

35:31.629 --> 35:33.840
I heard Nu-a is collaborating with SJ.

35:33.923 --> 35:34.924
Who's Nu-a?

35:35.007 --> 35:37.927
An artist who has the same style as him.

35:38.010 --> 35:39.804
A rival of his.

35:41.055 --> 35:43.182
"A rival"? You've got to be kidding.

35:43.266 --> 35:45.643
Hey, Nu-a's just copying me.

35:45.726 --> 35:49.313
At this rate, people will say
you're the one copying Nu-a.

35:49.397 --> 35:51.774
Do you want to go back to being a bum
like five years ago?

35:51.858 --> 35:55.278
- Why do you keep bringing up the past?
- So you'll be motivated!

35:55.361 --> 35:57.321
Do you really want to live like that?

35:58.322 --> 35:59.407
Jeez.

36:03.703 --> 36:05.705
It wasn't that bad.

36:08.624 --> 36:10.209
What are you on about?

36:16.632 --> 36:17.967
Hey.

36:18.050 --> 36:19.427
Let's make a bet.

36:19.510 --> 36:20.928
If you score 15 points first,

36:21.470 --> 36:23.556
I'll move
all the cabbages for you tomorrow.

36:24.682 --> 36:25.641
Really?

36:27.351 --> 36:29.353
- Come on.
- I'm game.

36:29.437 --> 36:31.230
You won't score a single point.

36:51.417 --> 36:53.502
Ja-gyeong!

36:56.505 --> 36:59.175
You reek of alcohol.

36:59.258 --> 37:02.053
Did you drink again?

37:02.136 --> 37:05.389
I want to make a doll with your stomach.

37:05.473 --> 37:07.975
Then I can squeeze it every day.

37:08.059 --> 37:10.186
Get washed up and go to bed.

37:10.269 --> 37:12.104
You have to go to work tomorrow.

37:12.688 --> 37:15.149
Just sleep inside, even if I'm late.

37:15.233 --> 37:17.568
Don't stay up waiting for me.

37:17.652 --> 37:19.612
I was out here because it was hot.

37:19.695 --> 37:21.697
Go and get washed up.

37:22.406 --> 37:23.783
Can't you wash me?

37:24.909 --> 37:27.870
- Wash me, Grandma.
- My goodness.

37:27.954 --> 37:29.956
- Give me a kiss.
- What's with you?

37:30.539 --> 37:31.749
- You've lost your mind!
- Come on.

37:31.832 --> 37:33.334
What's gotten into you?

37:34.085 --> 37:37.088
- Why?
- You stink! Go away.

37:37.171 --> 37:40.758
My goodness. Unbelievable.

37:40.841 --> 37:43.010
How much have you had to drink?

37:44.011 --> 37:45.096
My gosh.

38:01.237 --> 38:02.697
ARTIST GO-OH

38:05.449 --> 38:06.826
GO-OH'S SOLO EXHIBITION

38:08.411 --> 38:10.746
GO-OH, THE ILLUSTRATOR
WHO PAINTS BUILDINGS WITH SOUL

38:20.381 --> 38:22.300
WHAT EXCITES YOU THE MOST
ABOUT BUILDINGS?

38:25.219 --> 38:27.305
YOU DRAW NATURE AS WELL AS BUILDINGS
WHAT ARE YOUR INTERESTS?

38:27.388 --> 38:29.598
CAN YOU TELL US
ABOUT YOUR DRAWING PROCESS?

38:29.682 --> 38:33.227
WHY AREN'T THERE PEOPLE IN YOUR DRAWINGS?

38:33.311 --> 38:36.856
I LOVE THINGS THAT DON'T CHANGE
BUT PEOPLE CHANGE OR DISAPPEAR OVER TIME

38:36.939 --> 38:40.901
THAT'S WHY THERE ARE NO PEOPLE
OR TIME IN MY WORKS

38:59.920 --> 39:01.964
Ji-ung, our team leader
was looking for you.

39:02.048 --> 39:04.342
I know. He's calling me every ten minutes.

39:04.425 --> 39:05.760
Didn't you go home again?

39:05.843 --> 39:06.844
Do I smell?

39:06.927 --> 39:08.220
How many days has it been?

39:08.304 --> 39:09.638
It's only my fourth day.

39:09.722 --> 39:10.973
I told you to go home.

39:11.057 --> 39:13.517
Don't make it a habit
of living in the editing room.

39:13.601 --> 39:16.604
Mr. Park said he couldn't
go home at all when he was an assistant.

39:16.687 --> 39:19.231
Hey, don't listen to anything he says.

39:19.315 --> 39:21.734
There's nothing worth listening to.

39:23.694 --> 39:25.613
- Oh, right. Chae-ran.
- Yes?

39:25.696 --> 39:28.908
- Work with me on my next project.
- When I'm done with Mr. Park's.

39:28.991 --> 39:31.077
It's fine. I'm going to steal you away.

39:36.499 --> 39:37.917
Were you looking for me?

39:40.169 --> 39:42.588
Do you know what time it is?

39:43.798 --> 39:45.800
Let me get a proper break.

39:47.843 --> 39:51.680
I'm guessing that you
need me to work my ass off for something.

39:52.264 --> 39:53.599
You've gotten smart.

39:55.309 --> 39:56.852
I'm telling you in advance.

39:56.936 --> 39:59.230
I'm not doing documentaries
on people anymore.

39:59.855 --> 40:01.065
Why not?

40:01.148 --> 40:02.942
They're boring.

40:03.025 --> 40:05.444
I want something related
to the environment. It will be perfect.

40:05.528 --> 40:08.239
Environment? Don't you know
how tough that is?

40:08.322 --> 40:10.074
But they're fun.

40:10.157 --> 40:13.244
I heard Yun-jin doesn't want to do it.
Just give that to me.

40:16.038 --> 40:18.791
Fine. Do it. I'll give you that one.

40:19.959 --> 40:21.001
What?

40:22.253 --> 40:23.629
What's going on?

40:23.712 --> 40:26.340
What's gotten into you? Are you serious?

40:26.424 --> 40:28.175
Do one on people first.

40:28.259 --> 40:30.344
Then I'll let you do it. I swear!

40:30.428 --> 40:32.012
Jeez. I knew it.

40:32.096 --> 40:34.473
You'll never just let me
do something I want.

40:34.557 --> 40:37.184
It's a simple one. It's not even a series.

40:37.268 --> 40:40.563
Then you can get someone else to do it.
Like Mr. Han.

40:42.398 --> 40:44.108
Hey. Look at this.

40:45.109 --> 40:46.235
How about it?

40:56.871 --> 41:00.332
Someone who loves me deeply,
someone I can always be with--

41:00.416 --> 41:02.793
- Ridiculous.
- My gosh!

41:02.877 --> 41:04.503
What? What is it?

41:05.087 --> 41:06.213
What is it? Tell me.

41:06.297 --> 41:07.590
How could I not know?

41:07.673 --> 41:09.049
Why? Did you find Go-oh?

41:10.509 --> 41:12.803
Hey, isn't that Ms. Kook?

41:12.887 --> 41:16.182
I saw these videos before.
Why didn't I realize it was her?

41:16.265 --> 41:18.517
Hold on. Is that the view count?

41:18.601 --> 41:20.102
That's crazy.

41:20.186 --> 41:21.937
Ms. Kook was harsh back then too.

41:22.521 --> 41:24.607
She talks exactly the same way
as Mr. Jang.

41:24.690 --> 41:26.859
Totally. She seems
harsher in these videos.

41:26.942 --> 41:28.652
This kid's name is Ung.

41:28.736 --> 41:30.863
She was so mean to him.

41:30.946 --> 41:33.449
But Ung keeps fighting back.

41:33.532 --> 41:36.452
Those two fight like cats and dogs.

41:36.535 --> 41:40.456
But from what I remember,
Yeon-su's the one who starts the fight.

41:40.539 --> 41:42.124
- Unbelievable.
- Is that so?

41:42.208 --> 41:43.792
Totally.

41:44.376 --> 41:47.880
I have the feeling that Yeon-su
has a crush on Ung.

41:52.676 --> 41:53.677
Ms. Kook.

41:54.178 --> 41:55.387
Hello, Ms. Kook.

41:55.471 --> 41:57.014
Ji-un, that thing I asked for…

41:57.598 --> 41:58.432
Ms. Kook, when…

41:59.016 --> 42:02.811
Am I that similar to Mr. Jang?

42:02.895 --> 42:05.189
Who? You?

42:05.272 --> 42:08.025
Of course not.
You're much better than him.

42:08.108 --> 42:10.277
So I'm just as annoying as he is.

42:10.361 --> 42:13.113
- Of course not! We didn't mean that.
- No way!

42:13.197 --> 42:17.284
I think the producers
made you look mean in the video.

42:17.368 --> 42:20.663
Right. Did you sue them for this?
You really should.

42:20.746 --> 42:22.331
- Right!
- Yes, you should.

42:22.414 --> 42:24.542
What is it? Why are you all gathered here?

42:24.625 --> 42:25.793
Is there something fun?

42:25.876 --> 42:28.629
Do any of you know
how to get stuff like that deleted?

42:28.712 --> 42:31.674
Well, it's from a television network,
so you should talk to them.

42:31.757 --> 42:34.843
- Television? What's this about?
- Should I file a complaint?

42:34.927 --> 42:36.512
Are you gathering the data?

42:36.595 --> 42:38.806
Of course, we're getting
everything on Go-oh.

42:38.889 --> 42:41.559
What is it? Tell me what's going on.

42:41.642 --> 42:43.978
We have to hand over the files
by next week.

42:44.061 --> 42:46.230
I guess you have a lot of time
on your hands.

42:48.399 --> 42:50.150
- And Ye-in.
- Yes?

42:50.234 --> 42:52.319
It wasn't me. It was him.

42:53.237 --> 42:56.240
- What do you mean?
- He picked the fights first.

42:56.323 --> 43:00.119
- Ung was always the one who started it.
- Oh, I see.

43:00.869 --> 43:04.456
Right. What I meant was…

43:04.540 --> 43:07.376
What is it? Tell me.

43:07.459 --> 43:09.295
Come on. Tell me.

43:09.378 --> 43:12.131
I won't tell anyone,
so tell me what this is about.

43:14.800 --> 43:16.385
- No.
- Yes.

43:16.468 --> 43:17.928
Why do you always say no?

43:18.012 --> 43:20.514
Why would I shoot that again?

43:20.598 --> 43:23.309
Don't you see the views?
Look at the comments.

43:23.392 --> 43:26.145
This is the most popular documentary
on our channel.

43:26.228 --> 43:28.022
It's just trending for a while.

43:28.105 --> 43:30.482
Plus, it seems like
only kids are watching it.

43:30.566 --> 43:32.818
Do you know
what our director's saying these days?

43:32.901 --> 43:35.029
"We have to attract more young viewers."

43:35.112 --> 43:38.782
Can you come up with a better idea
to attract young viewers than this?

43:38.866 --> 43:42.286
Do we film anything that has
a lot of views and young viewers?

43:42.369 --> 43:43.537
Can't you just do it?

43:44.413 --> 43:48.626
Do you know why dating reality shows
are popular these days?

43:49.752 --> 43:52.588
It's even more dramatic
than any of the TV series.

43:53.172 --> 43:54.256
Look at this.

43:54.340 --> 43:56.967
There aren't any TV series
that's this entertaining.

43:57.051 --> 43:59.845
If we show how these kids
have changed after ten years,

43:59.928 --> 44:03.057
it'll be epic. I guarantee you.

44:03.140 --> 44:07.269
If we do a good job,
we'll get a totally popular documentary.

44:07.353 --> 44:09.980
But why would I film that?
You're the one who made it.

44:11.690 --> 44:13.233
I'm not young anymore.

44:13.901 --> 44:15.110
I'm old now.

44:15.194 --> 44:16.320
Plus…

44:20.824 --> 44:21.659
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

44:21.742 --> 44:23.160
Hey, Ji-ung!

44:23.952 --> 44:25.704
You must know them the best.

44:25.788 --> 44:28.791
Do you still keep in touch with them?

44:29.625 --> 44:32.002
How are they doing? I'm curious myself.

44:32.086 --> 44:34.088
It's been ten years.

44:35.506 --> 44:36.840
Have they changed a lot?

44:48.727 --> 44:50.020
They all say he's cute.

44:50.104 --> 44:51.689
This won't do.

44:52.272 --> 44:54.858
"I'm an acquaintance of Choi Ung."

44:55.526 --> 44:58.779
"He's still as weird as he is

44:59.405 --> 45:01.031
in this video."

45:02.783 --> 45:03.867
All right.

45:06.787 --> 45:08.747
Ung! You have a call!

45:12.167 --> 45:13.335
Ung!

45:14.878 --> 45:15.963
Jeez.

45:26.348 --> 45:27.599
Ung!

45:31.145 --> 45:33.981
Ung!

45:34.064 --> 45:35.774
Tell him I'll move the cabbages soon.

45:35.858 --> 45:38.986
- No, it's not that.
- Do I have to do it now?

45:39.486 --> 45:41.572
Look at it.

45:41.655 --> 45:43.240
What's with you?

45:43.323 --> 45:45.492
Come on. Get it. Hurry!

45:45.576 --> 45:46.869
What?

45:46.952 --> 45:48.704
Come on, answer it!

45:49.580 --> 45:50.747
Hello?

45:50.831 --> 45:52.916
It's hard to get in touch with you.

45:53.000 --> 45:55.669
I heard you work late at night,
but you wouldn't pick up.

45:55.752 --> 45:58.589
And I called you in the morning,
but you still didn't pick up.

45:58.672 --> 46:03.177
Oh, NJ. I didn't know I got a call. Hello.

46:03.260 --> 46:05.387
You must be busier than idol singers.

46:05.971 --> 46:08.348
I guess you must be busier
since the articles got out

46:08.432 --> 46:10.225
about me buying your drawing.

46:10.893 --> 46:15.314
Right. More people seem to
want to buy my drawings now. Thank you.

46:15.981 --> 46:17.858
Is that it, though?

46:18.984 --> 46:21.195
I want to see more of your work.

46:22.362 --> 46:25.866
- What are you doing today?
- Oh, I'm moving cabbages--

46:26.658 --> 46:27.743
What?

46:27.826 --> 46:29.203
Jeez!

46:31.538 --> 46:34.333
I'm actually moving cabbages--

46:35.000 --> 46:38.462
Do you want to meet up later today?
I want to take a look around your studio.

46:39.254 --> 46:40.964
Oh, today?

46:41.048 --> 46:44.176
Yes, today. I think I can end early.

46:44.843 --> 46:46.053
I see.

46:46.136 --> 46:47.763
Tell her to come.

46:47.846 --> 46:50.766
All right. Then let me know
when you're getting off work.

46:51.350 --> 46:53.769
- I'll call you later then.
- Okay.

46:58.398 --> 47:01.151
Oh, my god! This is crazy!

47:03.403 --> 47:06.698
- Were you staying in touch with NJ?
- This is the first time.

47:06.782 --> 47:09.535
When did you exchange numbers?

47:09.618 --> 47:11.578
She asked for my number first.

47:11.662 --> 47:13.539
She asked for your number? Why?

47:13.622 --> 47:16.208
I don't know. Get away from me.
You're scaring me.

47:16.291 --> 47:18.293
This is awesome! I can't believe it!

47:18.377 --> 47:21.964
This must be a dream.
Choi Ung had a phone call with NJ.

47:22.047 --> 47:23.298
- This is insane.
- But…

47:24.633 --> 47:27.928
She called because she wants
a free drawing, right?

47:29.054 --> 47:30.264
What?

47:30.347 --> 47:31.765
I mean…

47:32.391 --> 47:34.726
- "Is that it?" And then she said…
- Is that it?

47:34.810 --> 47:37.563
- I want to see more of your work.
- "I want to see more of your work."

47:38.605 --> 47:41.400
She wants a drawing for free, right?

47:42.442 --> 47:46.446
Ung. NJ just bought a building
worth 15 billion won last week.

47:46.530 --> 47:50.075
And just give her one if she asks.
Give her anything she wants.

47:50.158 --> 47:53.829
Just give her everything you have!

47:53.912 --> 47:56.039
Give her everything!

47:56.123 --> 47:58.458
Is NJ really coming here?

47:59.084 --> 48:00.586
I can't believe it!

48:01.420 --> 48:04.172
- What should I wear?
- Hey, let me see your hands.

48:05.299 --> 48:06.258
What for?

48:10.679 --> 48:13.473
If you go through my stuff again,
you're dead.

48:13.557 --> 48:15.892
I might die before that.
My heart's about to burst.

48:15.976 --> 48:18.854
I've been a fan since her trainee days.
So let me off this time.

48:18.937 --> 48:22.733
Do you think it makes sense
for you to be wearing that at home?

48:24.526 --> 48:25.819
I guess you're right.

48:26.320 --> 48:27.904
- Darn it. What do I wear?
- Jeez.

48:28.447 --> 48:29.781
There's nothing to wear.

48:30.574 --> 48:31.700
What?

48:32.451 --> 48:33.702
Why are there two of these?

48:33.785 --> 48:35.370
- Hey, that's--
- It's tacky.

48:37.664 --> 48:38.915
No way.

48:39.750 --> 48:41.293
Is that a matching couple's shirt?

48:41.918 --> 48:43.670
What with the long face?

48:44.254 --> 48:45.339
Shut up.

48:45.422 --> 48:47.132
You wore matching t-shirts?

48:47.215 --> 48:48.550
How cute.

48:49.885 --> 48:51.345
A leather jacket.

48:52.429 --> 48:53.513
Would it be too much?

49:09.613 --> 49:11.490
Hello. Are you with someone?

49:11.573 --> 49:12.616
Yes.

49:26.797 --> 49:28.090
Mr. Jang?

49:36.473 --> 49:38.517
This is pretty awkward.

49:39.184 --> 49:40.686
What are you doing here alone?

49:40.769 --> 49:42.979
Well, what does it look like?

49:43.063 --> 49:45.273
Your reservation table is this way.

49:45.357 --> 49:46.900
Oh, all right.

50:16.221 --> 50:17.222
Ms. Kook Yeon-su?

50:20.100 --> 50:21.727
You're Choi Ung, right?

50:22.227 --> 50:24.938
You were in that documentary.
The worst student.

50:26.523 --> 50:29.276
- No, I'm not.
- Come on. You are!

50:29.359 --> 50:31.737
Hey, he said it's not him. Let's go.

50:33.780 --> 50:37.576
I'm sure it's him!
He looks exactly the same.

50:37.659 --> 50:39.035
Mr. Kang Min-su?

50:39.119 --> 50:39.995
Yes. Please sit.

50:47.461 --> 50:49.045
You finally came.

50:49.671 --> 50:52.132
I'm sorry about last time.

50:52.883 --> 50:56.344
- It's fine.
- Well, then shall we…

51:00.432 --> 51:02.434
I still wanted to see you

51:03.101 --> 51:05.228
even after being stood up four times

51:05.854 --> 51:07.898
because I wanted to check something.

51:08.565 --> 51:10.275
- What--
- We first set a date

51:10.358 --> 51:12.736
to meet in Yeoido at 7 p.m.,
but you didn't come.

51:12.819 --> 51:15.989
And then we set a date
to meet at Hongdae at eight.

51:16.072 --> 51:18.325
You stood me up both times
because of work.

51:18.408 --> 51:20.827
Well, I--

51:20.911 --> 51:22.329
The third was on a weekend.

51:22.412 --> 51:23.830
We were to meet at three,

51:23.914 --> 51:26.917
but you called at five-to
and canceled because of work.

51:27.000 --> 51:28.251
The fourth was the lunch yesterday.

51:28.335 --> 51:31.505
We were supposed to meet for 30 minutes
during lunch at your company building,

51:31.588 --> 51:33.381
but you forgot that due to work.

51:33.965 --> 51:37.093
I guess you're doing all the work
at your company.

51:37.177 --> 51:39.304
Mr. Kang…

51:39.387 --> 51:43.266
So I told your friend for the fifth time
that I wanted to see you.

51:44.684 --> 51:47.521
I just couldn't give up like that.

51:49.856 --> 51:52.734
I was worried
that you wouldn't turn up again.

51:52.818 --> 51:54.236
But thank you for coming.

51:55.570 --> 51:58.365
I'm sorry about last time.

51:59.199 --> 52:00.534
I was wondering

52:01.117 --> 52:04.871
if you were worth
all the time I was wasting,

52:06.248 --> 52:07.916
but I see that you're not.

52:09.209 --> 52:11.670
- What?
- This might seem petty…

52:14.464 --> 52:16.675
That's right.
This is why I wanted to see you.

52:17.843 --> 52:19.135
I hope you meet a nice man.

52:20.887 --> 52:21.805
Wait…

52:22.472 --> 52:25.350
I'm not sure you'll be able to though.

52:26.017 --> 52:26.977
Bye, then.

53:08.852 --> 53:11.104
Did you hear everything?

53:12.939 --> 53:14.107
No.

53:19.154 --> 53:23.033
You say that, but that smile
on your face bothers me.

53:23.116 --> 53:24.576
I could hear everything.

53:24.659 --> 53:27.203
I'd appreciate it
if you could pretend you didn't.

53:27.787 --> 53:29.915
Do you mean about the blind date itself,

53:29.998 --> 53:32.208
or about how you were rejected?

53:32.292 --> 53:34.085
Which do you mean?

53:37.672 --> 53:39.507
Your food is ready, sir.

53:39.591 --> 53:40.926
Thank you.

53:41.009 --> 53:42.052
Enjoy.

53:46.306 --> 53:47.724
Seems like you're eating alone.

53:48.308 --> 53:49.935
Mind if I join you?

53:51.102 --> 53:54.064
Wouldn't it be awkward
since we're wearing the same shirt?

53:54.856 --> 53:57.859
I think it'll be weirder to eat separately
with the same shirt on.

53:57.943 --> 54:01.237
I'll pay for my own food,

54:01.321 --> 54:02.822
so just let me sit here.

54:06.201 --> 54:07.452
Fine, then.

54:21.967 --> 54:25.387
Stupid rain… My shoot isn't ending.

54:25.470 --> 54:27.222
I'm so sorry.

54:27.305 --> 54:29.808
Could I head over tomorrow morning?

54:46.616 --> 54:49.035
Are you going to keep being such a bore?

54:49.119 --> 54:51.621
I never considered myself boring.

54:54.624 --> 54:57.168
Do you drink alone like this often?

54:57.252 --> 54:59.421
Sometimes, after work.

54:59.504 --> 55:02.924
I see. I guess you
must be an empty shell too.

55:03.758 --> 55:05.176
I don't understand.

55:06.302 --> 55:10.390
My teammates say that you and I are alike.

55:11.266 --> 55:13.727
I'm not sure. Only our shirts are alike.

55:13.810 --> 55:16.187
I was kind of startled when I heard that.

55:16.938 --> 55:19.107
As I was looking at you,

55:19.190 --> 55:23.403
I told myself that
I was much more human than you.

55:24.487 --> 55:27.490
Are you drunk?
Or are you pretending to be?

55:28.324 --> 55:29.909
I don't get drunk.

55:29.993 --> 55:32.704
The amount of liquor I can hold
has increased over time.

55:46.217 --> 55:48.136
There really isn't anything to talk about.

55:49.179 --> 55:51.598
I can talk endlessly about work,

55:51.681 --> 55:53.141
but I don't want to right now.

55:53.224 --> 55:55.477
I'm ready to hear anything work-related.

55:55.560 --> 55:57.896
Well, what should I talk about?

56:03.443 --> 56:04.778
That shirt.

56:04.861 --> 56:06.154
How much was it?

56:06.237 --> 56:09.282
I used a discount coupon
and got it really cheap.

56:09.365 --> 56:11.284
I'd be upset if I paid more for it.

56:11.367 --> 56:12.660
I paid full price for it.

56:14.245 --> 56:15.497
That's good to hear.

56:17.540 --> 56:19.292
But isn't it kind of amazing?

56:19.375 --> 56:21.711
Wearing the same shirt
and coming to the same place.

56:22.879 --> 56:26.049
It's my first time wearing
the same clothes as someone else.

56:26.132 --> 56:27.509
This is still quite awkward.

56:28.384 --> 56:30.136
You never wore matching t-shirts?

56:30.220 --> 56:32.263
I hate pathetic stuff like that.

56:35.517 --> 56:38.728
I used to hate pathetic things too.

56:42.732 --> 56:44.400
But I guess you've

56:45.151 --> 56:46.444
done it before.

56:47.362 --> 56:50.073
Well, you know…

56:50.156 --> 56:52.283
Sometimes you become someone else.

56:54.035 --> 56:55.995
- Is that so?
- I knew it.

56:56.663 --> 56:59.958
I really am more human than you.

57:00.500 --> 57:01.709
That again?

57:02.502 --> 57:05.130
I used to be so childish.

57:22.397 --> 57:25.692
Can I have a glass of that wine too?

57:25.775 --> 57:28.236
Wine and soju aren't a great match.

57:28.319 --> 57:30.989
It's fine. I enjoy all kinds of alcohol.

57:44.752 --> 57:46.045
Darn it.

57:46.129 --> 57:47.964
Gosh, Eun-ho.

58:02.520 --> 58:03.688
Jeez.

58:18.244 --> 58:19.287
So…

58:20.580 --> 58:22.540
just like ten years ago…

58:36.721 --> 58:38.181
Eun-ho!

58:39.557 --> 58:40.558
Darn it!

58:49.275 --> 58:50.568
Jeez!

58:51.277 --> 58:52.612
What time is it?

58:53.530 --> 58:55.114
Hey, Eun-ho!

58:55.657 --> 58:57.158
Aren't you going to get the door?

58:57.242 --> 59:01.120
…it all happened
regardless of my intentions again.

59:02.372 --> 59:03.414
Who…

59:08.670 --> 59:09.712
As if it had to happen.

59:13.383 --> 59:16.261
I thought I'd never
be involved with him again.

59:17.720 --> 59:19.347
It's better to just give up.

59:19.430 --> 59:22.976
Why? Are they still on bad terms?
Do they still fight all the time?

59:27.188 --> 59:30.858
The thing about love and hate is that
there is a very thin line between them.

59:30.942 --> 59:32.986
They're two sides of the same coin.

59:33.069 --> 59:34.946
What are you on about?

59:35.029 --> 59:36.781
They were together

59:36.864 --> 59:39.117
for about five years.

59:39.200 --> 59:42.495
They actually dated?

59:54.048 --> 59:55.300
Darn it!

01:00:04.267 --> 01:00:07.562
- Will you close the door again?
- And they broke up pretty badly.

01:00:08.855 --> 01:00:11.190
They hurt each other so much

01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:13.901
that they'll probably never
see each other again.

01:00:21.367 --> 01:00:28.374
I KNOW WHAT YOU DID LAST SUMMER

01:00:40.553 --> 01:00:42.096
- What did you say?
- Let's break up.

01:00:42.180 --> 01:00:44.515
Do you really have to do this now?

01:00:44.599 --> 01:00:46.100
Why shouldn't I?

01:00:46.184 --> 01:00:47.477
This is the fifth time.

01:00:47.560 --> 01:00:48.686
Two of them were you.

01:00:48.770 --> 01:00:50.980
- Do you really mean it? Gosh.
- Yes.

01:00:52.106 --> 01:00:52.982
You're at it again.

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:55.068
You just need everything to go your way.

01:00:55.151 --> 01:00:56.569
What? What is it this time?

01:00:56.653 --> 01:01:00.156
You always make conclusions
by yourself without talking to me.

01:01:00.782 --> 01:01:02.784
You always thought that
about me, didn't you?

01:01:02.867 --> 01:01:05.828
- I'm the selfish bitch, aren't I?
- Stop that.

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:08.373
You just don't want to be
the one to break up.

01:01:08.456 --> 01:01:11.250
- Yeon-su.
- I'll be a bitch, just like you wanted.

01:01:11.334 --> 01:01:13.086
So let's end this, okay?

01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:18.049
Yeon-su!

01:01:21.469 --> 01:01:22.762
I bought you that shirt.

01:01:47.036 --> 01:01:48.746
I wouldn't have come to see you
if it wasn't for this.

01:01:48.830 --> 01:01:49.706
Is that so?

01:01:50.540 --> 01:01:52.750
- What?
- So how was it to see her again?

01:01:52.834 --> 01:01:55.628
- I don't even remember what I said.
- Are you nuts?

01:01:56.671 --> 01:01:58.089
- Do you like me that much or not?
- Hey, don't.

01:01:58.172 --> 01:01:59.132
Stop following me.

01:02:00.007 --> 01:02:05.680
I think someone is
stealing your car right now.

01:02:05.763 --> 01:02:08.057
They look like a couple
that they're together.

01:02:08.141 --> 01:02:09.100
You bastard.

01:02:09.183 --> 01:02:10.810
It's been five years after all.

01:02:10.893 --> 01:02:13.146
What if I was serious
and didn't act childish?

01:02:14.021 --> 01:02:15.648
Would you have managed?

01:02:17.191 --> 01:02:21.654
Subtitle translation by: Ju-young Park
